{"study_accession":"PRJNA597718","secondary_study_accession":"SRP238793","title":"scRNA-seq of peripheral blood from West Nile Virus-infected patients","description":"We profile the peripheral blood of patients infected with West Nile Virus with divergent disease-trajectories (West Nile Encephalitis, West Nile Fever, and asymptomatic) during relatively acute infection and at a convalescent timepoint (~90-days later) using single-cell RNA sequencing in an effort to uncover determinants of disease progression and flesh out the landscape of infection. In the blood of the infected patients, stratified cell-states involved in acute viral infection resolve into more homogenous states at the follow-up blood draws, A dramatic shared transcriptional shift between the primary blood-draws during acute infection and the 90-day follow-ups in all observed compartments allows us to highlight multiple cell-type and cell-state-specific patterns of gene expression. Overall design: Single-cell RNA on patient samples infected with West Nile Virus","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":54,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN13681893","study_accession":"PRJNA597718","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"182442_081518_PBMC_scRNA-seq_2018_Thawed_2","description":"182442_081518_PBMC_scRNA-seq_2018_Thawed_2","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM4232622","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-12-26","attributes":[["source_name","PBMCs"],["disease","West Nile Encephalitis"],["cell_type","PBMC"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR10767066","experiment_accession":"SRX7440990","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":282304073,"base_count":20043589183,"first_public":"2021-12-26","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM4232622: 182442_081518_PBMC_scRNA-seq_2018_Thawed_2 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN13681894","study_accession":"PRJNA597718","blood_class":"pbmc","